The legal texts come from the Portalul legislativ of the Romanian Ministry of Justice:

  Sursa: Portalul legislativ al Ministerului Justiției, https://legislatie.just.ro,
  read through Internet Archive captures (https://web.archive.org), retrieved 28-29 October 2026.

They are official texts of normative acts of Romania. Romanian copyright law excludes official texts of a
legislative, administrative and judicial nature, and their official translations, from protection (Legea nr. 8/1996
privind dreptul de autor și drepturile conexe, art. 9 lit. b).

Changes made by Lexifina: each consolidated form was converted to one Markdown file per article, one paragraph per
line; typography (cedilla and comma-below letters, spaces, quotes, dashes, footnote markers) was normalised; the
portal's amendment notes and editorial notes were removed from the text and used only to credit the amending act;
and the forms were arranged as git commits credited to the acts that made each change. The wording of the law was
not changed. The Ministry of Justice does not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
